90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Energy peers: EV/EBITDA 4.7 vs 6.9 and P/FCF 8.1 vs 14.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 59% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are attractive: an FCF yield of 12.4% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 8.2% (vs the 8% bar).","The 29 covering analysts target $167 on average, 14% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 23% clears the cost of capital of 8.0% by 15pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.31).","It converts 42% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 2.02x, but a weak Piotroski score of 3/9 and high accruals (-9.8% of assets).","ROE of 17% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.7x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 7pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.0% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.4x net debt to EBITDA ($3.4B of cash against $7.9B of debt), with interest covered 27.2x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -4.2% over 3 years, 15.5% over 5 years and 10.0% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 34%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 14.9% a year over five years.","Capex runs only 0.1x depreciation (2.1% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 57, clearing the bar for a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 5.3% on average."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 98%.","It returns 6.1% a year to shareholders (3.3% in buybacks and 2.8% in dividends).","The share count has grown 2.0% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 36 consecutive years."],"people":["With about 3,400 employees, each generates about $6.7M of revenue, 3.3x the Energy median, and productivity has risen 10.2% a year.","That works out to $2.8M of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.8M (1x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (3/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $64K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":91,"head":"Invest: trades 52% below fair value of $305; ROIC 23.5% vs WACC 8.0%.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 52, gates 13/24)","Trades 52% below fair value of $305","ROIC 23.5% vs WACC 8.0%","FCF margin 42.3%","Revenue grew 15.5%/yr over 5y"],"cons":["Piotroski F-score 3/9"],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":259.45,"vc":{"base":305.24,"base_src":"dcf","bear":234.89,"bull":411.51,"alt_median":117.53,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.5971,"dispersion":0.2689,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 160% above the other models' median ($118)"]},"med":{"pe":13.3952,"ev_ebitda":6.86,"pfcf":14.299,"pb":1.6885,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0754,"div_yield":0.0371}},"ticker":"EOG","date":"2026-11-06"}